{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46295-gods-with-unique-powers-that-don-t-seem-to-fit-within-the-current-purvew-system","id":46295,"title":"Gods with unique powers that don't seem to fit within the current Purvew system.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-10T09:06:00-08:00","id":46295,"title":"Gods with unique powers that don't seem to fit within the current Purvew system.","content":"Some Gods seem to have powers that don't seem to fit within any of the current Purviews. How do you think those powers should be dealt with?<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are more examples, but I'm a little pressed for time, so I'll just list the examples that are immediately on my mind. Feel free to list any others you can think about.<br /> <br /> Interestingly enough, all my examples currently come from the Devas.<br /> <br /> 1.) Shiva's &quot;Destructo Eye.&quot; Shiva has a third eye that he typically keeps closed. Because if he opens it, whatever that eye sees goes &quot;Kaboom!&quot; He has been known to open that eye to destroy powerful enemies and sometimes even people who just pissed him off. This doesn't seem to fit into any existing power set that I can think of. How would you deal with this ability of Shiva's if you were going to have him use it?<br /> <br /> 2.) Shiva and Kali both are known for their destructive dances as well. That's all that really seems to be involve. They dance and the world starts falling apart around them. I suppose this MAY be a use of the Earth Purview, causing violent earthquakes, but I believe Fire and a whole lot of other bad stuff comes into play as well. Once again, if you were running a scene with Kali and/or Shiva in it and he or she (or, God forbid, both of them) started dancing, how does this work?<br /> <br /> 3.) As was discussed on the Virgin Goddess thread, Brahma and Sarasvati are known to create their Scions by basically just thinking them into existence. Thanks to the Percy Jackson books, we even have reason to believe that Athena could do this as well. How would you stat up this ability to create an entire human/God hybrid from sheer force of will?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":679,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","user":"unnatural1","date":". 01-10-2014, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T09:27:15-08:00","id":46306,"title":"","content":"1) Could be the Chaos Purview Avatar<br /> <br /> 2) Chaos, Fire, Earth or Death Avatars<br /> <br /> 3) Forge/Artistry/Creation/Industry or Health Avatar<br /> <br /> Avatars generally cover this kinda thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T09:46:30-08:00","id":46321,"title":"","content":"1) Shiva's Destructo Eye is actually statted up as a Relic in JSR's Reliquary supplement, on their Downloads page.<br /> <br /> 2) This answer is entirely dependant on JSR's Artistry Purview, so will not be too useful to those who don't use it. Back when Artistry came out, I had a talk with John and Anne about Gods like Sarasvati creating Relic Songs using the Artistry Purview the way Hephaesthus uses it to create Relic Weapons. That is, a musical performance, that when properly performed by the Scion to whom it is bound by Fate (so every random individual singing a few bars doesn't set it off), can perform miracles. My intent with this suggestion, was to recreate various Indian legends of musicians so talented they could call storms and fire with nothing but song. I would say that Shiva and Kali's dance is a similar relic. A set of dance steps bound by Fate to the divine duo, that when performed properly and only by them, act as Weapons of Mass Destruction.<br /> <br /> 3) I agree with Telgar here. I know John and Anne don't agree with this particular use of The Creator, but I will have to disagree with them. Forging a Scion into existence (a single one per use, mind you) should be something the Avatar of Artistry can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T10:55:50-08:00","id":46354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>unnatural1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46295-gods-with-unique-powers-that-don-t-seem-to-fit-within-the-current-purvew-system#post46295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) Shiva's &quot;Destructo Eye.&quot; Shiva has a third eye that he typically keeps closed. Because if he opens it, whatever that eye sees goes &quot;Kaboom!&quot; He has been known to open that eye to destroy powerful enemies and sometimes even people who just pissed him off. This doesn't seem to fit into any existing power set that I can think of. How would you deal with this ability of Shiva's if you were going to have him use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds familiar.<br /> <img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/03/Cyclopsclassic.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.) Shiva and Kali both are known for their destructive dances as well. That's all that really seems to be involve. They dance and the world starts falling apart around them. I suppose this MAY be a use of the Earth Purview, causing violent earthquakes, but I believe Fire and a whole lot of other bad stuff comes into play as well. Once again, if you were running a scene with Kali and/or Shiva in it and he or she (or, God forbid, both of them) started dancing, how does this work? </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, Dancing is the Deva equivalent to Nanomachines (son.)<br /> <br /> Which means it's magic and they don't have to explain shit. Shiva and Kali start dancing, roll dice to see what breaks and how hard. Don't try to figure it out.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T12:50:37-08:00","id":46434,"title":"","content":"Hmf...Shiva's eye was so destructive it wiped out a layer of our current reality. (i.e. one of Brahma's heads/faces)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T12:51:25-08:00","id":46435,"title":"","content":"Balor of the Tuatha has a destructo-eye as well, so this phenomena isn't limited to just gods. Actually I recall them giving certain titans (like the aforementioned Balor) unique abilities in various writeups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T15:32:05-08:00","id":46543,"title":"","content":"I think these powers are boons that only those Gods (or Titans know). God of Nuclear Power? Get Sun and re-skin it to fit the theme. Any other Power it would fit a God can be placed within a Purview quite easily.<br /> <br /> There are Gods with great powerful boons due to the amount of Fatebinding that they have.<br /> <br /> 1) The Eye Beam, quite common in Legend actually. I would go with an Flare Missile that is way more powerful.<br /> <br /> 2) Probably Landslide, with bonus power when dancing due to Fatebinding.<br /> <br /> 3) Genesis, pure and simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T16:27:35-08:00","id":46576,"title":"","content":"1) Relic.<br /> <br /> 2) Artistry or Relic (similar to a maiming relic; not a physical thing but still has a supernatural effect).<br /> <br /> 3) Artistry Avatar or Health Avatar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-10T22:52:50-08:00","id":46759,"title":"","content":"If they make stats for the minor gods of pantheons, I would like to see a variation of the Psychopomp purview called the Dream Purview, because of the Greek God of Dreams, Morpheous(?). While the Psychopomp purview deals with going to Terra Incognita and the Underworld, the Dream purview can do the same thing with dreams. OP could probably use the Dream Contract of Changeling the Lost as an inspiration for making the purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T06:42:59-08:00","id":46862,"title":"","content":"I played a god of dreams in a Scion home game. In canon what little effect gods have over dreams takes the form of a handful of scattered boons over like 4 different purviews and one single magic spell. We all thought this was bullshit due to: 1) there being actual gods of DREAMS (Morpheus), and 2) there being actual Titans of Sleep and Dreams (Hypnos, Selene meddled with it too). To make it worse they created this supplement in France called &quot;We are but mere Mortals&quot; or somesuch where an entire cult of people called the Key of Morpheus had various dream powers bestowed from that god. We ended up using someone's fan-made Dream Purview from off of the original forums to fill in the gap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T07:57:56-08:00","id":46901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46295-gods-with-unique-powers-that-don-t-seem-to-fit-within-the-current-purvew-system?p=46434#post46434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmf...Shiva's eye was so destructive it wiped out a layer of our current reality. (i.e. one of Brahma's heads/faces)</div> </div> </div> </div>So he has the Ultimate Nullifier in his forehead. Neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T10:49:39-08:00","id":46968,"title":"","content":"*shrugs* If I remember it right, it was the reason why we can't readily perceive all of reality.<br /> <br /> The sheer destructiveness of some of the powers that certain Hindu deities were supposed to have, rivaled or surpassed the power of Thor's hammer. It's kinda crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T08:46:10-08:00","id":48996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/46295-gods-with-unique-powers-that-don-t-seem-to-fit-within-the-current-purvew-system?p=46306#post46306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Could be the Chaos Purview Avatar<br /> <br /> 2) Chaos, Fire, Earth or Death Avatars<br /> <br /> 3) Forge/Artistry/Creation/Industry or Health Avatar<br /> <br /> Avatars generally cover this kinda thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Telgar said. By the time you're dealing with full-blown deities the basic rules of the game have long since been thrown out the window. Avatars are the standard answer to &quot;how do I create narrative effect X?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}